Hi there!

  Don't normally read this group, don't normally play NetHack since I've already
ascended a couple of the classes (namely Wizard, Priest, and Knight, in that
order), but it's still a good game and I was playing tonight.
  I've got a question for you source gurus out there, so if you're not one of
them, consider this a spoiler warning.

  Kicked up a Samurai and started bouncing around, got my dog killed on the
first floor of the Mines.  Bit a dwarf who bit back.  So I go back upstairs 
cos I'm not tough enough to do the Mines by myself yet Next floor, I find a
hobbit who's not interested in fighting and also a nice scroll, which as it
turns out is a scroll of destroy armor.  Great.  Find another scroll...
  Punished?  But I hadn't done anything!  Right, That Does It!  Thammy now
decides to run as deep as he can go, killing everything and everybody in his
path.  The peaceful hobbit is his first victim, quickly disposed of.  Caution
thrown to the wind, Thammy kicks up a door to be confronted with an angry
shopkeeper.  Thammy looks him up and down and pays the 400 zorkmids, then
proceeds into the shop.  He is wearing a cursed ring of invisibility.
  The shop looks something like below.
          -----
          +@  |
          |   |
          |   |
          |   |
          |X  |
          -----
  X is Thammy's position, the door has been reconstructed.  What happens now,
what causes Thammy to quietly raise his Yumi, and what my question is finally
all about is:  @, the shopkeeper's position.  What is he doing there?
  Thammy fires...  The shopkeeper, get this, does not _budge_!  He simply
stands there and lets me gun him down.  Takes a while, but he dies...  Why?
The version is 3.1.3.

